## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design a beginner OTCA path with privacy by design, geohash-based location masking, and per-tenant residency.

## Key Concepts

- Ingest-time privacy and per-tenant opt-in

- Geohash granularity and redaction strategy

- Regional topics and date-partitioned Parquet

- End-to-end testing for privacy, QoS, and data freshness

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode for ingest
function ingest(event) {
  // redact precise coords, derive geohash4
  const hash = geohash.encode(event.lat, event.lon, 4);
  const out = {
    tenant_id: event.tenant_id,
    event_type: event.event_type,
    timestamp: event.timestamp,
    geohash4: hash,
    session_id: event.session_id
  };
  publish(out);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate audits for tenants with opt-in vs opt-out?

- How would you monitor latency and privacy violations in production?

## Why This Is Asked
This question probes practical OTCA telemetry design for AI inference with explainability, focusing on tenancy, privacy, and compatibility rather than volume. It requires mapping events, streaming paths, retention, and a lightweight schema-registry and tests, while introducing explainability data as a new angle.

## Key Concepts
- Cross-tenant AI telemetry
- Privacy-preserving ingestion (hashing, redaction)
- Per-tenant residency and retention
- Schema registry compatibility
- Basic QoS testing

## Code Example
```javascript
function redact(input){
  const crypto = require('crypto');
  const h = crypto.createHash('sha256');
  h.update(String(input));
  return h.digest('hex');
}
